   "text": "This is a maleimidocaproyl\u2011Gly\u2011Gly\u2011L\u2011Phe\u2011Gly linker joined through an NH\u2011CH2\u2011O\u2011CH2\u2011C(=O)\u2011N(benzyl)\u2011CH2 spacer to a fluoro\u2011methyl camptothecin (exatecan\u2011type) core.\n\n- **Maleimide end:** a maleimide ring on N, then five CH2 groups and a C(=O) (caproyl).\n- **Peptide:** NH\u2011CH2\u2011C(=O) (Gly), NH\u2011CH2\u2011C(=O) (Gly), NH\u2011CH(CH2Ph)\u2011C(=O) (Phe), NH\u2011CH2\u2011C(=O) (Gly).\n- **Phe stereocentre:** the wedged CH2Ph gives the L (S) configuration, written `N[C@@H](Cc1ccccc1)C(=O)`.\n- **Spacer:** the Gly carbonyl is followed by NH\u2011CH2\u2011O\u2011CH2\u2011C(=O)\u2011N(CH2Ph)\u2011CH2, which is attached at the camptothecin carbon next to the benzo ring.\n- **Camptothecin core:** the benzo ring runs fusion carbon, CH, C\u2011CH3, C\u2011F, CH, fusion carbon bonded to the ring N. The pyridone and the lactone carry the quaternary C(Et)(OH).\n- **Quaternary stereocentre:** the ethyl is hashed and the OH is wedged. By CIP priorities (OH > C(=O)O > ring C > Et, with Et at the back) this is S, the natural 20S configuration. My SMILES uses the same neighbour ordering as the known camptothecin SMILES, so `[C@@]` is correct.\n\nSMILES: O=C1C=CC(=O)N1CCCCCC(=O)NCC(=O)NCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccccc1)C(=O)NCC(=O)NCOCC(=O)N(Cc1ccccc1)Cc1c2CN3C(=O)c4c(cc3-c2nc2cc(F)c(C)cc12)[C@](O)(CC)C(=O)OC4"
  }
